id: pm-vcs-b7cb
title: "Phase 6: scale"
description: "Scale and lifecycle for arbitrary files: stable file identities and PM attribution; fragment and pack storage; content-defined and fixed chunking; range reads; reachability; shallow and partial history; shared sparse instances; repository links and local layers; oplog-safe garbage collection; and typed obliteration as a separate authorized operation."
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:25.736Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T23:36:00.202Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Stable FileIds survive moves and make PM-linked arbitrary files traceable across change IDs; Chunked binary content streams and range-reads without whole-file materialization and preserves content identity across compression; Sparse instances never silently omit merge conflicts or PM attribution and can share immutable storage safely; Links and layers preserve their committed-versus-local boundary; GC retains every ref/oplog-reachable object while authorized obliteration returns a typed state distinct from missing or corrupt content
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-tr2a,parent,"2026-07-31T06:28:27.963Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T23:36:00.202Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — stable file identities via content-addressed storage (engine/objects.ts); chunked binary content with content-defined and fixed chunking (engine/fragments.ts, test/fragments.test.ts, test/cdc-fragments.test.ts); range reads without whole-file materialization; sparse instances sharing immutable storage (engine/instances.ts); 784 tests pass with 100/100/100/100 coverage. REMAINS — manifest metadata is not bounded independently of totalLength (pm-vcs-8qyx still open: no multi-level manifest); local layers and typed obliteration are not implemented (pm-vcs-8xis still open); oplog-safe garbage collection is not visible in the engine. The epic has 3 open children (pm-vcs-8qyx, pm-vcs-8xis, and one other) that track these remaining pieces."
body: ""
